// Upward-drifting random walk WITHOUT counter: terminates with probability 1/2.
// Phi_g has rational PHANTOM fixpoints, e.g. (1 + X)/(1 - 2X), whose exit part (= 1) wrongly suggests
// almost-sure termination; the least fixpoint 1/2 + (3/2) X/(1 - X) has infinite mass as well.
// Sandwich: finite-mass subinvariants (Rule B) from below, a superinvariant with constant tail from above.
nat x;
x := 1;
while (x > 0) {
  {x := x + 1} [2/3] {x := x - 1}
}
?Pr[true]
